  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126363,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 373,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:24:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126364,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 373,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Three main histopathological patterns have been described {22197859; 23521538}. The acanthotic pattern demonstrates acanthosis of the matrix epithelium and includes whorls of epithelium that may show differentiation into onychocytes (nail plate cells); the associated nail plate is thickened. The papillomatous pattern demonstrates papillomatous projections of matrix-derived epithelium associated with a thickened nail plate; there are cavities within the nail plate. The keratogenous pattern demonstrates a thickened keratogenous zone and forms a channel along the nail plate. The cells in the keratogenous zone show delayed maturation into onychocytes, which occurs in the channel at the distal aspect of the nail unit. None of these patterns have any dermal component, which helps in the differentiation from onychomatricoma and other nail unit tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:24:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126365,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 373,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:24:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
